// src/lsp_hover.pdx -- libpdx-pds-parser.R225.M8 (paideia-os#2689)
//
// LspHover: LSP-embed hover-query surface. Given a cursor byte
// offset into a semantic-shell source buffer, resolves the token
// under the cursor to a 128-byte HoverResponse record carrying the
// inferred (type, effect-row, capability-row) triple -- the three
// summary rows a user hovering a token in the line editor cares
// about: WHAT it is (R225.M1 HmCore principal type), WHAT it DOES
// (R224.M3 EffectRow), and WHAT it NEEDS (R224.M4 CapRow).
//
// =============================================================================
// SCOPE
// =============================================================================
//
// R225 is the typechecker umbrella (design/terminal/semantic-shell-
// language-plan.md section "R225 -- Unified HM type checker across
// three sub-languages"). M1 (HmCore) landed Robinson/Damas-Milner
// kernel. M2 (RowTypes) landed Remy-style row polymorphism. M4
// (EffectUnify) landed effect-row JOIN. M6 (RankCheck) landed the
// rank-restriction gate. M7 (DiagReport) landed typed-error
// diagnostic reporting with source spans. R225.M8 (THIS module)
// lands the HOVER surface the LSP-embed consumer (R220.M9 LSP
// transport side) calls once per cursor-rest event in the line
// editor (R229.M6 LineEditor / R229.M7 ViMode) to render the
// three summary rows.
//
// The hover surface runs USER-SPACE because the shell runs
// user-space; raw M8 holds NO .bss state (every HoverResponse
// record is caller-owned); the module touches no kernel KIND and
// consumes no capability. See caps.decl R225.M8 band note.
//
// At raw M8 the type / effect / capability triple is served from a
// 10-entry DEMO TABLE in `.rodata` keyed on the ASCII token under
// the cursor; the forward-path landing M8.1 wires the real HmCore
// / EffectUnify / CapRow elaborator surfaces so the triple is
// derived from the live typing environment per cursor-rest. The
// demo table satisfies the acceptance corpus of 10 sample
// expressions (shell builtins + base-type identifiers; see §7 of
// `design/shell/lsp-hover.md`) without any dependency on an
// elaborator run having completed yet.
//
// Position in the substrate graph:
//
//   LineEditor (R229.M6) / ViMode (R229.M7) raises CURSOR_REST
//     event with (buffer_ptr, buffer_len, cursor_byte) tuple
//   -> _lh_query(buffer_ptr, buffer_len, cursor_byte, out, out_cap)
//      returns packed_u64 = (DR_RECORD_BYTES << 32) | status
//   -> on OK: `out` holds a 128-B HoverResponse record
//   -> _lh_render_lsp_json(record, 128, out_json, out_json_cap)
//      returns a one-line LSP `Hover` response payload
//   -> LSP transport (R220.M9) wraps it in the `textDocument/hover`
//      reply envelope and emits over the LSP transport socket.
//
// Out of scope at raw M8 (deferred to M8.1+ follow-ups):
//   * HmCore / EffectUnify / CapRow wire-up: raw M8 serves the
//     triple from the demo table; M8.1 replaces the lookup with a
//     call into the elaborator's live typing environment keyed on
//     the AST node under the cursor (R221.M5 Ast).
//   * `_lh_set_env(te_ref)` -- stash a R229.M3 TypeEnv pointer in
//     a module-private .bss slot so M8.1's elaborator-wire-up can
//     reach the scheme store without rethreading the arg list.
//   * `_lh_byte_offset_to_line_column(buffer, len, byte_off)
//     -> packed(line_u32, col_u32)` -- parallels R225.M7.2's
//     DiagReport line/column resolver; the LSP range emission at
//     raw M8 uses `line=0, character=byte_offset` as the byte-level
//     fallback (same convention DiagReport uses pre-M7.2).
//   * Multi-token hover chaining via `next_hover_ref` at [+120]:
//     reserved at raw M8 for the M8.2 session-local hover-queue
//     landing (parallels DiagReport's M7.1 queue head).
//   * UTF-8 identifier charset: raw M8 accepts the ASCII identifier
//     subset `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]` (the ten demo tokens plus the Unicode-
//     agnostic shell builtin surface). M8.3 extends to the TR#31
//     identifier profile over NFC-normalised bytes.
//
// Status band 0x5E00..0x5EFF carved on the next kilo-step boundary
// past Wave 130's R229.M9 Renderer (0x5D00..0x5DFF). Grep-confirmed
// virgin outside this module + caps.decl + the design doc.
//
// =============================================================================
// HoverResponse RECORD WIRE FORMAT -- 128 BYTES EXACTLY
// =============================================================================
//
//   [+0x00]  u32    magic              = 'HOVR' (0x52564F48 LE)
//   [+0x04]  u32    token_byte_offset  into caller's SOURCE buffer
//                                       (NOT the NFC-normalised buffer;
//                                       Q-A5 invariant)
//   [+0x08]  u32    token_byte_length
//   [+0x0C]  u32    flags              bit 0 LH_FLAG_TYPE_KNOWN
//                                       bit 1 LH_FLAG_EFFECT_KNOWN
//                                       bit 2 LH_FLAG_CAP_KNOWN
//                                       bit 3 LH_FLAG_IS_IDENT
//                                       bits 4..31 reserved
//   [+0x10]  u8[32] type_name_inline   NUL-padded; stop-at-NUL on render;
//                                       empty => omit from message
//   [+0x30]  u8[32] effect_row_inline  same shape; e.g. "{io,fs}"
//   [+0x50]  u8[32] cap_row_inline     same shape; e.g. "{tty,fs}"
//   [+0x70]  u64    reserved
//   [+0x78]  u64    next_hover_ref     0 at raw M8 (M8.2 queue link)
//
// Total: 128 bytes == 0x80 == 2^7. Record addressing is `shl r, 7;
// add r, base` (power-of-two stride; no `imul` pitfall). The three
// 32-byte inline strings sit at contiguous offsets 0x10 / 0x30 /
// 0x50 so the demo-table hit path writes them in a single 96-byte
// byte-count loop from a 112-byte table-entry triple at `entry+16`.
//
// Magic 'HOVR' = 0x52564F48 LE reads as "HOVR" in a hex-dump
// sequential scan (byte[0]=0x48 'H', byte[1]=0x4F 'O', byte[2]=0x56
// 'V', byte[3]=0x52 'R'). The magic u32 fits imm32 with bit 31
// clear (0x52 = 0101_0010; high bit of byte 3 is 0) so direct
// `cmp reg, imm32` and `mov reg, imm32` are sign-extension-safe.
//
// =============================================================================
// PUBLIC API
// =============================================================================
//
//   _lh_init() -> ()
//     Bare `ret`. M8 holds NO .bss state (every HoverResponse record
//     is caller-owned; the session-local hover-queue head slot
//     lands at M8.2). Kept for parallelism with the parser-family
//     init-hook convention (`_dr_init` R225.M7, `_rc_init` R225.M6,
//     `_lc_init` R227.M4, `_rd_init` R229.M9).
//
//   _lh_query(buffer_ptr, buffer_len, cursor_byte, out, out_cap)
//                                                     -> packed_u64
//     Resolve the token at `cursor_byte` into the HoverResponse
//     record at `out`.
//       rdi = buffer_ptr    source bytes (ASCII identifier charset
//                           at raw M8; the ten demo tokens; see §7
//                           of design/shell/lsp-hover.md).
//       rsi = buffer_len    bytes in `buffer_ptr`.
//       rdx = cursor_byte   caret position; may equal buffer_len
//                           (end-of-line); will be clamped to
//                           buffer_len-1 for the scan if so.
//       rcx = out           destination 128-byte record buffer.
//       r8  = out_cap       caller's buffer capacity.
//       rax = packed_u64 = (LH_RECORD_BYTES << 32) | status.
//
//     Status codes: LH_OK (0), LH_ERR_BAD_INPUT (0x5E00; any
//     required pointer == 0), LH_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL (0x5E01;
//     out_cap < 128), LH_ERR_CURSOR_OOB (0x5E02; cursor_byte >
//     buffer_len), LH_ERR_NO_TOKEN (0x5E03; cursor sits on a
//     non-identifier byte with no identifier byte adjacent).
//
//     On LH_ERR_NO_TOKEN the record is still zero-filled and the
//     magic is still stamped so a downstream consumer can tell the
//     response is well-formed; the token_byte_* fields are 0 and
//     the three 32-B strings are all-NUL. Status returned so the
//     caller can skip the LSP response round-trip.
//
//     Register plan: 5 input args fit the SysV x64 6-arg ceiling
//     (per sysv_x64_7arg_unsafe_body_b1708.pdx + design/compiler/
//     lambda-arity-stack-spill.md §4.4). The function has TWO
//     nested CALLs (into `_lh_h_scan_token` and `_lh_h_table_lookup`)
//     and therefore requires a callee-save frame.
//
//   _lh_render_lsp_json(record_ptr, record_len, out, out_cap)
//                                                     -> packed_u64
//     Serialize the record to an LSP `Hover` payload (one-line
//     JSON object; the LSP transport wraps it in the standard
//     `textDocument/hover` reply envelope with the request id):
//       {"contents":{"kind":"markdown","value":"**type**: <t>\n
//        **effects**: <e>\n**capabilities**: <c>"},"range":{"start":
//        {"line":0,"character":<n>},"end":{"line":0,"character":<n>}}}
//     Fields with empty inline strings (first byte == NUL) are
//     omitted from the markdown body (e.g. no `**effects**` line
//     when effect_row_inline is empty).
//
//     Returns packed_u64 = (bytes_written << 32) | status.
//     Status codes: LH_OK (0), LH_ERR_BAD_INPUT (0x5E00),
//     LH_ERR_BAD_RECORD (0x5E05; record_len < 128 or magic
//     mismatch), LH_ERR_RENDER_OVERFLOW (0x5E06).
//
// =============================================================================
// INTERNAL HELPERS (module-private pure leaves)
// =============================================================================
//
//   _lh_h_is_ident(byte) -> u64
//     Returns 1 iff byte in [a-zA-Z0-9_-] (0x30..0x39 | 0x41..0x5A
//     | 0x5F | 0x61..0x7A | 0x2D), else 0. Pure leaf; no CALL.
//
//   _lh_h_scan_token(buffer, len, cursor) -> packed_u64
//     Finds the identifier-char contiguous span straddling the
//     cursor via grow-left-then-right. Returns packed_u64 =
//     (token_offset << 32) | token_length. On no token the packed
//     value is 0 (both zero). Pure leaf; no CALL (is_ident is
//     inlined-via-call so one nested CALL fires inside this helper;
//     see Alt-Flow note below).
//
//     Alt-Flow note: `_lh_h_scan_token` CALLs `_lh_h_is_ident`
//     repeatedly inside its two loops; that makes the scan helper
//     NOT a pure leaf by the convention. The scan helper therefore
//     carries a minimal 2-push + sub-rsp,8 frame (rbx = cursor
//     scratch; r12 = len; rsp%16==0 at nested CALL per 8+16+8=32).
//     Simpler alternative at M8.2+: fold is_ident into scan_token
//     as four inline cmp-range checks (loses the pure-leaf
//     advantage of is_ident; keeps scan_token pure).
//
//   _lh_h_table_lookup(token_ptr, token_len, out_record) -> flags
//     Walks the 10-entry `_lh_demo_table` at `.rodata`. For each
//     entry: compare entry[+0..+16] (NUL-padded name) against
//     token_ptr[0..token_len] with length-equal + byte-equal
//     constraints; on hit, byte-copy 96 bytes from entry[+16] to
//     out_record[+16] (the three 32-B strings land at contiguous
//     record offsets 0x10 / 0x30 / 0x50). Returns the flag bits
//     (LH_FLAG_TYPE_KNOWN | _EFFECT_KNOWN | _CAP_KNOWN) on hit, 0
//     on miss. Pure leaf; no nested CALL (byte-copy is inlined as
//     a 96-count mov_b loop).
//
//   _lh_h_emit_lit(src, src_len, out, out_cap, pos) -> new_pos
//     Byte-copy `src_len` literal bytes to `out+pos`. Validates
//     `pos + src_len <= out_cap`; returns `out_cap + 1` sticky
//     overflow sentinel on failure. Same shape as DiagReport's
//     `_dr_h_emit_lit`; copied here to keep the two modules'
//     helper surfaces disjoint (parallels R225.M6 RankCheck's
//     and R225.M7 DiagReport's independent emit helpers). Pure
//     leaf; no CALL.
//
//   _lh_h_emit_cstr(src, max_bytes, out, out_cap, pos) -> new_pos
//     Byte-copy from `src` up to `max_bytes` or first NUL. Same
//     shape as DiagReport's `_dr_h_emit_cstr`. Pure leaf; no CALL.
//
//   _lh_h_emit_u32_dec(value, out, out_cap, pos) -> new_pos
//     Emit variable 1..10 decimal digits for `value` low 32 bits
//     via greedy subtraction over the 10-entry _lh_pow10 table.
//     Value 0 emits '0'. Same shape as DiagReport's
//     `_dr_h_emit_u32_dec`. Pure leaf; no CALL.
//
// =============================================================================
// paideia-as ENCODER DISCIPLINE (ABSOLUTE)
// =============================================================================
//
//   - No `test rN, rN` -- every zero-check is `cmp reg, 0; je/jne`.
//   - No `and rN, imm64` -- band values 0x5E00..0x5EFF fit imm32
//     with bit 31 clear.
//   - No 2-op `imul r, imm` -- 128-byte record stride is `shl r, 7`;
//     128-byte table-entry stride is `shl r, 7`; 32-byte string
//     stride is `shl r, 5`; 4-byte u32 stride is `shl r, 2`.
//   - No multiline `pub let = "..."` -- single-line justifications.
//   - Module basename `LspHover` matches `lsp_hover.pdx`.
//   - Labels prefixed `lh_` for public entries + the token helpers
//     and `lh_h_` for the four emit / scan / lookup helpers
//     (grep-confirmed unique against every landed parser-tier
//     prefix: u8n_, gi_, wp_, cl_, ast_, sm_, fh_, sch_sig_,
//     cmd_sig_, fi_, afs_, cmdreg_, dm_, ds_, pl_, pl_lam_, rp_,
//     fo_, sgr_, ws_, ha_, st_, ll_, cc_, er_, cr_, ls_, lp_, hm_,
//     rt_, eu_, dl_, se_, te_, jc_, h_, le_, vi_, ml_, ir_, rc_,
//     rd_, dr_, lc_). Never bare `loop`/`if`/`let`/`fn`/`ret`/
//     `done`.
//   - All `cmp reg, imm` immediates (0, 1, 10, 16, 32, 48, 64, 80,
//     96, 112, 128, status codes 0x5E00..0x5E06, '0'=0x30,
//     '9'=0x39, 'A'=0x41, 'Z'=0x5A, 'a'=0x61, 'z'=0x7A, '_'=0x5F,
//     '-'=0x2D, powers of 10 up to 10^9=0x3B9ACA00) fit imm32
//     with bit 31 clear so direct `cmp reg, imm32` is sign-
//     extension-safe.
//   - Byte loads via `xor r,r; mov_b r,[base + idx * 1]` on
//     reg+reg or `xor r,r; mov_b r,[base + imm_disp]` on reg+disp.
//     u32 loads via `xor r,r; mov_d r,[base + imm_disp]` (zero-
//     extends per SDM Vol.1 3.4.1.1). u32 stores via `mov_d`.
//     u8 stores via `mov_b`.
//   - No chained-displacement operands (precedent: span_map.pdx,
//     diag_report.pdx, rank_check.pdx). Three-term address
//     computations are pre-computed into a register via `mov; shl;
//     add` sequences.
//   - Cross-module .bss not written (zero `.bss` at raw M8).
//   - Register-liveness audit:
//       `_lh_init`         bare ret; zero pushes; pure leaf.
//       `_lh_h_is_ident`   zero pushes; pure leaf; four cmp-range
//                          checks.
//       `_lh_h_scan_token` 2 pushes (rbx = buffer / r12 = cursor-
//                          scratch) + sub rsp,8 align; two nested
//                          CALLs into _lh_h_is_ident; rsp%16==0 at
//                          every CALL (entry 8 + 16 + 8 = 32).
//       `_lh_h_table_lookup` zero pushes; pure leaf; the 96-byte
//                          byte-copy on hit is inlined.
//       `_lh_h_emit_lit`   zero pushes; pure leaf.
//       `_lh_h_emit_cstr`  zero pushes; pure leaf.
//       `_lh_h_emit_u32_dec` zero pushes; pure leaf.
//       `_lh_query`        6 pushes (rbx/rbp/r12/r13/r14/r15 = 48B)
//                          + sub rsp,8 align; TWO nested CALLs
//                          (_lh_h_scan_token + _lh_h_table_lookup);
//                          rsp%16==0 at every CALL (entry 8 + 48 +
//                          8 = 64).
//       `_lh_render_lsp_json` 6 pushes + sub rsp,8 align; multiple
//                          nested CALLs (_lh_h_emit_lit /
//                          _lh_h_emit_cstr / _lh_h_emit_u32_dec);
//                          rsp%16==0 at every CALL.
//
// =============================================================================
// FORWARD PATH
// =============================================================================
//
//   R225.M8.1  Replace the demo-table lookup with a live elaborator
//              query against R225.M1 HmCore / R224.M3 EffectRow /
//              R224.M4 CapRow via the AST node identified by the
//              cursor-byte -> AST-node resolver (R221.M5 Ast at
//              `_ast_find_by_span`).
//   R225.M8.2  `.bss` session-local hover-queue head slot +
//              `_lh_enqueue(record)` enqueuer (parallels
//              DiagReport M7.1).
//   R225.M8.3  TR#31 identifier profile over NFC-normalised
//              bytes (R221.M1 UTF-8 decoder + R221.M2 grapheme
//              iterator wire-up).
//   R225.M8.4  `_lh_set_env(te_ref)` stash of a R229.M3 TypeEnv
//              pointer in a module-private .bss slot so M8.1 can
//              reach the scheme store without rethreading the arg
//              list.
//   R225.M8.5  60-expression acceptance corpus + golden LSP JSON
//              outputs per `design/shell/lsp-hover.md` §8.
//   R225.M8.6  Kernel-side wire-up at the LSP transport dispatch
//              tier (R220.M9; reads `_lh_render_lsp_json` for the
//              LSP envelope payload).
//   R225.M8.7  Chained hover payload: when the token under cursor
//              is a lambda-literal `fn (...) ->` body, chain hover
//              records for the lambda's argument types via
//              `next_hover_ref` into an M8.2 queue the LSP consumer
//              drains.
//
// =============================================================================
// Upstream: paideia-os#2689 (THIS ticket, R225.M8), parent umbrella
// paideia-os#2489 (R225 umbrella). Design doc:
// design/shell/lsp-hover.md. Related plans:
// design/terminal/semantic-shell-language-plan.md section R225.M8,
// design/shell/hm-algorithm-w-core.md (R225.M1 HmCore type names),
// design/shell/effect-polymorphism.md (R224.M3 EffectRow),
// design/shell/capability-row-typing.md (R224.M4 CapRow),
// design/shell/diagnostic-reporting.md (R225.M7 DiagReport parallel
// emitter discipline), design/shell/span-map-nfc.md (R221.M6 Q-A5
// source-span invariant), design/shell/line-editor-emacs.md
// (R229.M6 cursor-rest event source), design/shell/line-editor-vi.md
// (R229.M7 vi-mode cursor-rest event source).

module LspHover = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 1 -- STATUS CODES (returned in low 32 of packed_u64)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Band 0x5E00..0x5EFF carved on a kilo-step boundary past Wave
  // 130's R229.M9 Renderer (0x5D00..0x5DFF). Grep-confirmed virgin
  // at R225.M8 landing time (see caps.decl R225.M8 band note).

  pub let LH_OK                     : u64 = 0
  pub let LH_ERR_BAD_INPUT          : u64 = 0x5E00
  pub let LH_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL      : u64 = 0x5E01
  pub let LH_ERR_CURSOR_OOB         : u64 = 0x5E02
  pub let LH_ERR_NO_TOKEN           : u64 = 0x5E03
  pub let LH_ERR_UNKNOWN_TOKEN      : u64 = 0x5E04
  pub let LH_ERR_BAD_RECORD         : u64 = 0x5E05
  pub let LH_ERR_RENDER_OVERFLOW    : u64 = 0x5E06

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 2 -- FLAG BITS + MAGIC + LAYOUT CONSTANTS
  // ==========================================================================

  pub let LH_FLAG_TYPE_KNOWN        : u64 = 1
  pub let LH_FLAG_EFFECT_KNOWN      : u64 = 2
  pub let LH_FLAG_CAP_KNOWN         : u64 = 4
  pub let LH_FLAG_IS_IDENT          : u64 = 8

  // 'HOVR' little-endian: H(0x48) O(0x4F) V(0x56) R(0x52) ->
  // u32 LE = 0x52564F48. Bit 31 clear; imm32-safe.
  pub let LH_MAGIC                  : u64 = 0x52564F48

  // Record layout.
  pub let LH_RECORD_BYTES           : u64 = 128
  pub let LH_NAME_BYTES             : u64 = 32
  pub let LH_TRIPLE_BYTES           : u64 = 96
  pub let LH_TABLE_ENTRIES          : u64 = 10
  pub let LH_TABLE_ENTRY_BYTES      : u64 = 128
  pub let LH_TABLE_NAME_BYTES       : u64 = 16

  pub let LH_OFF_MAGIC              : u64 = 0
  pub let LH_OFF_TOKEN_OFFSET       : u64 = 4
  pub let LH_OFF_TOKEN_LENGTH       : u64 = 8
  pub let LH_OFF_FLAGS              : u64 = 12
  pub let LH_OFF_TYPE               : u64 = 16
  pub let LH_OFF_EFFECT             : u64 = 48
  pub let LH_OFF_CAP                : u64 = 80
  pub let LH_OFF_RESERVED           : u64 = 112
  pub let LH_OFF_NEXT               : u64 = 120

  // Render output caps (callers may pass larger).
  pub let LH_LSP_MIN_CAP            : u64 = 512

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3 -- STATIC TABLES (.rodata)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Powers of 10 (u32) for the decimal emitter's greedy subtraction.
  // All fit imm32 with bit 31 clear. Mirrors DiagReport's `_dr_pow10`
  // (independent copy; the two modules intentionally keep disjoint
  // helper surfaces so each ships standalone).

  pub let LH_POW10_COUNT            : u64 = 10

  pub let _lh_pow10 : [u32; 10] = [
    0x3B9ACA00,                              // 1_000_000_000
    0x05F5E100,                              // 100_000_000
    0x00989680,                              // 10_000_000
    0x000F4240,                              // 1_000_000
    0x000186A0,                              // 100_000
    0x00002710,                              // 10_000
    0x000003E8,                              // 1_000
    0x00000064,                              // 100
    0x0000000A,                              // 10
    0x00000001                               // 1
  ] @align(8)

  // ==========================================================================
  // SECTION 3.1 -- DEMO TABLE (10 x 128-byte entries, .rodata)
  // ==========================================================================
  //
  // Each entry is 128 bytes stride (power of two; `shl r, 7`
  // addressing):
  //   [+0..+16]   u8[16] name       (NUL-padded; length <= 15)
  //   [+16..+48]  u8[32] type       (NUL-padded; length <= 31)
  //   [+48..+80]  u8[32] effect     (NUL-padded)
  //   [+80..+112] u8[32] cap        (NUL-padded)
  //   [+112..+128] u8[16] reserved  (NUL-padded)
  //
  // The 96-byte (type, effect, cap) triple at [+16..+112] matches
  // the record's layout at [+16..+112] exactly, so a hit path
  // byte-copies 96 bytes with a single inline count loop.
  //
  // The ten entries are the raw-M8 acceptance corpus per
  // design/shell/lsp-hover.md §7. Each name is lowercase ASCII;
  // the identifier charset in the scan path (`[a-zA-Z0-9_-]`) is
  // the superset.

  pub let _lh_demo_table : [u8; 1280] = [
    // ----- Entry 0: name="x" -> type="u64", eff="{}", cap="{}" -----
    0x78, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,     // name
    0x75, 0x36, 0x34, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,     // type
    0x7B, 0x7D, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,     // effect
    0x7B, 0x7D, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
